An android program built for API 21, the lowest Compose runs on and the
lowest the gradle-free build accepts. Below API 24 d8 desugars Java 8
language features into the classes that use them, reading the libraries'
classes from its classpath to do so, the libraries are pre-dexed for that
level, and the APK carries a v1 (JAR) signature beside its v2 one, since a
device before Nougat reads only v1. The recorded run builds all of that.

The harness builds what the program generated, and the API level it builds
for is the one the manifest declares: it used to build every golden for API
26, whatever its `minSdk`, and the build now refuses a manifest that
declares another level from the one it was handed.
-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    kotlin {
        android(minSdk=21)
    }
}

component counter ui.node {
    var count = 0
    var seen list[int] = []
    ui.vbox {
        ui.text(value="Pressed {count} times")
        ui.button(text="Press", @click {
            count = count + 1
            seen.push(count)
        })
        for var n = seen {
            ui.text(value="{n}")
        }
    }
}

ui.window(title="API 21") {
    counter
}
